Skip the 4 generic_early_init FDT driver scans that find nothing on our board
(cppc/hsm/reset/suspend): each re-walks the whole device tree, and OpenSBI's
libfdt walking dominates NOEL-V RTL simulation wall time. Our DTB has no such
nodes, so these are functional no-ops -- removing them lets the sim reach the
post-sbi_platform_early_init boot path in tractable time.

DEBUG/sim aid: this disables the SBI system-reset / HSM-suspend / CPPC driver
probing, so revert for a production firmware that needs those.

--- a/platform/generic/platform.c
+++ b/platform/generic/platform.c
@@ -257,10 +257,6 @@
 		if (rc)
 			return rc;
 
-		fdt_cppc_init(fdt);
-		fdt_hsm_init(fdt);
-		fdt_reset_init(fdt);
-		fdt_suspend_init(fdt);
 	}
 
 	if (!generic_plat || !generic_plat->early_init)
